 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Shoshana Gordon/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Nvidia (Nasdaq: NVDA) announced that it will acquire open-source AI platform Hugging Face for $12.93 billion.

 Why it's the BFD: This is a massive validation of open-source AI, by a chip design giant known for its work with closed-model companies like Anthropic and OpenAI.

 It also comes just a month after Hugging Face was hacked by OpenAI models gone rogue, in what's become a major security wakeup call for the industry. ROI: Hugging Face had raised around $400 million in VC funding, most recently at a $4.5 billion valuation in 2023.

 Backers include Lux Capital, Addition, Sequoia Capital, Coatue, Menlo Ventures, Salesforce Ventures, and Nvidia. Flashback: I interviewed Hugging Face CEO Clem Delangue at last year's Axios BFD event. Here's the video .

 Behind the scenes: Hugging Face approached Nvidia about a deal, but had other bidders.

 In addition to the purchase price, Nvidia will pay up to $1 billion in employee retention bonuses. The bottom line: "This is another example of Nvidia's longer term goal: to be the top open AI model player. In the release, Nvidia emphasized Hugging Face's role in supporting open weight AI models, or those models with weights that are public and can be tinkered with by the end user." — Madison Mills, Axios 

 
 
