 🌲 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios Elliott Investment Management is lining up against Deutsche Telekom's efforts to merge with American arm T-Mobile US, in which it holds a 55% stake.

 The activist investor has built a "sizable stake" in Deutsche Telekom, according to Bloomberg , and opposes the deal. T-Mobile US has around a $200 billion market cap, despite its stock being down 26% over the past year, and a tie-up would create the world's largest mobile operator.

 
 
